<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Anglo-Dutch War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1652–1654</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-dutch-wars">Anglo-Dutch Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Anglo-Dutch War of 1652–1654 was a naval war between the Commonwealth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> over trade and shipping, sharpened by the English Navigation Act of 1651. It was fought almost entirely at sea, in battles such as the Kentish Knock, Portland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheveningen">Scheveningen</a>. The Treaty of Westminster of 1654 ended it on terms favourable to England.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-anglo-dutch-war.jpg" alt="First Anglo-Dutch War" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Abrahamsz Beerstraaten · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Scheveningen_(Slag_bij_Ter_Heijde)(Jan_Abrahamsz._Beerstraten).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
